__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Market data is regenerable, so it is not the record: the run manifest pins
# the exact bytes by hash, and data_import.py rebuilds the CSVs byte-for-byte
# from the trading-systems parquet cache. Committing ~29MB of it would add
# weight to a repo whose trust asset is a hash chain, for no integrity gain.
# (Coen, 2026-08-18. The recovery path is a re-fetch, which is hours of
# sequential API calls, not minutes -- see the vault note before relying on it.)
#
# BTCUSD_1d.csv and ETHUSD_1d.csv predate this rule and stay tracked; git
# ignores only untracked files, so they are unaffected. Use `git add -f` if a
# file here ever genuinely belongs in history.
data/*.csv

# SP4 Task P1: content-addressed sim cache for gauntlet's registry-wide
# clustering re-simulations (pipeline/simcache.py). Purely derived -- every
# entry is reproducible from the registry, the pinned data and engine.py's
# ENGINE_REV -- and it grows with every gauntlet run, so it is not the record.
simcache/

# 2026-09-13 (Coen): the registry and pipeline are the public trust asset;
# plans, run logs, unify notes, diagnostics, prompt files and the raw
# discovery queue are internal. Durable copy: stewartandco-agents/hubs/
# intelligence/research-layer-internals. Dated design docs, addenda and
# docs/notes stay tracked (pre-registrations the tests and README cite).
docs/plans/
docs/runs/
docs/unify/
docs/diagnostics/
docs/PROMPT-*.md
sources/discovery_queue.jsonl
sources/*.bak-*
